<title>UK: BOE invites fixed rate ops, shortage 800 mln stg.</title>
<headline>BOE invites fixed rate ops, shortage 800 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England around of fixed rate money market operations to offset a revised forecast shortage of 800 million stg.</p>
<p>The residual shortage is 290 million stg, taking earlier operations into account.</p>
<p>The repo rate is unchanged at 6.0 percent. The operations will comprise repos to April 23 and 25 and outright offers of bills maturing on or before April 25.</p>
</text>
